    "go": {
      "notes": [
        "The Go toolchain is installed from official go.dev archives. Version 1.27.3 contains the eMudhra certificate incident response. Platform SHA-256 values come from https://go.dev/dl/?mode=json&include=all.",
        "Go ships NO musl tarballs — the glibc archive is statically linked and runs on musl too, so the linux-*-musl canonical keys are absent and the installer falls back to the glibc sibling (linux-x64-musl → linux-x64, linux-arm64-musl → linux-arm64).",
        "integrity is the object form ({ value, src, date }) — value is `sha256-<hex>` (the publisher checksum shape), src the go.dev release manifest URL, date the pin day. install-tool.mjs parses the hex-after-prefix form and verifies before extract."
      ],
